#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md:6
msgid "The `quote!` macro"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md:8
msgid ""
"The **`quote`** crate provides the `quote!` macro, which is a powerful "
"templating engine for generating Rust code. It lets you write standard Rust "
"syntax and interpolate existing code from variables in scope:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md:15
msgid "// e.g. \"Student\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md:16
msgid "// Generate a TokenStream using standard Rust syntax as a template:\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md:21
msgid "\"My name is {}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md:25
msgid "// Convert to proc_macro::TokenStream:\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md:30
msgid ""
"**Interpolation:** Use `#var_name` to insert a variable (like an identifier, "
"type, or other token stream) directly into the template."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md:32
msgid ""
"**Repetitions:** Use `#(#var_list),*` to expand a list of variables "
"separated by commas, similar to how repetitions work in declarative macros."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md:37
msgid ""
"Note that `quote!` returns a `proc_macro2::TokenStream`. We call `.into()` "
"at the end of our procedural macro function to convert it to a standard "
"`proc_macro::TokenStream` for the compiler."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md:40
msgid ""
"Highlight how clean this makes code generation. Instead of manually pushing "
"string slices or tokens, you write literal Rust code blocks with templates."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/quote-macro.md:42
msgid ""
"Mention that repetition is often useful when iterating over all fields of a "
"struct."
msgstr ""
